      "user_id": 1,
      "message": "How do I grow rice?",
      "response": "Rice grows best in warm, humid conditions (25-35 C) in soil that holds water. It needs lots of water â€” transplant seedlings into a flooded field and split nitrogen in three doses (transplanting, tillering, panicle initiation). Harvest about 120-140 days after sowing.",
      "language": "en",
      "engine": "knowledge-base",
      "_id": "c14b3371-49b4-4c6d-8394-c10a36f890f9",
